02:23:17.475 NOT AUTHENTICATED: a migration seed is a u32, so it identifies a pending
02:23:17.475   migration rather than proving who is on the far end. It is single-use.
02:23:17.476 SET-FIELD PROBE IS ON - which by now means 'the channel answers at all'. The
02:23:17.476   flag is a misnomer kept for the launch line: without it Session::handle
02:23:17.476   returns nothing for every packet, so the migration hello goes unanswered and
02:23:17.476   the client freezes on 'Connecting...'.
02:23:17.477   With it on, this channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
02:23:17.477   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
02:23:17.477   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
02:23:17.477   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
02:23:17.477   script Say. Equipment, mobs and the Say are BUILT BUT UNCONFIRMED on screen.
